Setting Up Jenkins Master-Agent Architecture
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Understand the concept and benefits of Jenkins master-agent architecture
Install and configure Jenkins on a Linux system
Set up Jenkins agent nodes on the same machine using different ports
Establish secure communication between Jenkins master and agent nodes
Verify proper connectivity and job distribution between master and agents
Configure agents to execute build jobs independently
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with file permissions and user management in Linux
Basic knowledge of networking concepts (ports, localhost)
Understanding of what Jenkins is and its basic functionality
Experience with text editors like nano or vim
