Task 6: Monitor and Manage Agent Performance
Subtask 6.1: Check Agent System Resources
Create a monitoring job to check agent resources:

Create job: agent-monitoring
Label Expression: linux
Execute shell:
#!/bin/bash
echo "=== Agent System Monitoring ==="
echo "Date: $(date)"
echo "Uptime: $(uptime)"
echo "Memory usage:"
free -h
echo "Disk usage:"
df -h /home/jenkins-agent/
echo "Running processes:"
ps aux | grep jenkins | head -5
echo "=== Monitoring Complete ==="
Subtask 6.2: Configure Agent Offline Behavior
Go to Manage Jenkins → Manage Nodes and Clouds
Click on linux-agent-1
Click Configure
Under Availability, select Take this agent offline when idle
Set In demand delay: 1 minute
Set Idle delay: 5 minutes
Save the configuration
Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Agent Cannot Connect
If the agent shows as offline:

# Check SSH connectivity
sudo -u jenkins ssh -i /var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/jenkins_agent_key jenkins-agent@localhost

# Check Jenkins agent log
sudo tail -f /var/log/jenkins/jenkins.log

# Restart Jenkins service
sudo systemctl restart jenkins
Issue 2: Permission Denied Errors
# Fix ownership issues
sudo chown -R jenkins-agent:jenkins-agent /home/jenkins-agent/

# Check SSH key permissions
sudo chmod 600 /var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/jenkins_agent_key
sudo chmod 644 /var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/jenkins_agent_key.pub
Issue 3: Java Not Found on Agent
# Install Java on agent user environment
sudo apt install -y openjdk-11-jdk

# Add Java to agent user's PATH
echo 'export JAVA_HOME=/usr/lib/jvm/java-11-openjdk-amd64' | sudo tee -a /home/jenkins-agent/.bashrc
echo 'export PATH=$JAVA_HOME/bin:$PATH' | sudo tee -a /home/jenkins-agent/.bashrc
