Conclusion
In this lab, you have successfully implemented a Jenkins master-agent architecture on a single Linux machine. You learned how to:

Install and configure Jenkins master server
Set up agent nodes with proper SSH communication
Establish secure connections between master and agents
Verify job distribution and execution across agents
Monitor agent performance and resource usage
This master-agent architecture is crucial for scaling Jenkins in production environments. It allows you to distribute build workloads across multiple machines, isolate different types of builds, and provide better resource utilization. The skills you've gained here form the foundation for managing larger, more complex Jenkins deployments in enterprise environments.

The architecture you've built demonstrates how Jenkins can efficiently manage multiple build environments while maintaining centralized control and monitoring through the master node.
